    "chunk_text": "THE INDUSTRIAL DISPUTES ACT, CHAPTER 131 OF THE LEGISLATIVE ENACTMENTS OF CEYLON1956 REVISED EDITION\n\n07 Employees inclusive of Mrs. Rathnawali Mallika de Joeth, No. 45/2, Daladawatta Road, Thalpitiya South, Wadduwa. of the one part\n\nand\n\nSTATEMENT OF MATTER IN DISPUTE\n\nThe matter in dispute between the aforesaid parties is \u2013\n\n\u201cWhether the 7 of\ufb01cers mentioned in the schedule below amongst the 30 of\ufb01cers who were placed in Grade III Class III from 04.03.1987 have been caused injustice by,\n\n(1) not being placed in Grade III Class II as at 01.01.1988 (2) not being placed in Grade III Class I as at 01.01.1991 and (3) not being placed in the salary levels relevant for each Grade.\n\nin accordance with Ministry of Finance letter bearing No. MF2/1154/60/3 dated 23.10.1991, and if such injustice has been caused, to what relief they are entitled.\u201d\n\n01. Mrs. Rathnawali Mallika de Joeth 02. Mrs. H. D. N. D. Siriwardena 03. Mrs. G. T. M. Indrani Thanthrige 04. Mrs. B. M. K. Karunaratne 05. Mrs. G.K. K. Weerasinghe 06. Mr. I. L. Herath 07. Mr. Stanley Weerasinghe H. M. D. N. K. WATALIYADDA, Commissioner General of Labour.\n\nDated at the Of\ufb01ce of the Commissioner General of Labour,Colombo,on this 15th day of May, 2025.\n\nEOG 06 \u2013 0028/2\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA."
